	"title"		"Remake Map"
	"description"		"[b]Bad starting spot? Remake the map with one button - same settings, same whiskers, new island.[/b]

Rolled an island with no room to build, no ore nearby or a dock in a bad place? Starting over normally means going back to the menu and setting everything up again, and the starting whiskers you picked are gone. This mod adds a [b]Remake map[/b] button for the first day of a new colony.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Same new-game settings: map size, island sizes, extra and barren islands, scenario, difficulty and every other choice you made
[*]Same starting whiskers: the crew you picked comes along
[*]New random map: a fresh map seed every time, so you really get a different island
[*]Click twice: the first click arms the button, the second one remakes, so a stray click can't throw your colony away
[*]The button sits above the bottom toolbar on day 1 of a new colony and disappears when day 2 starts; loading screens and menus cover it like the rest of the game UI
[*]Does nothing in the background
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Only in a colony you just started: after loading a save there is no button, because the game only remembers the settings of your most recent new game
[*]The new colony keeps the same colony name
[/list]

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-remakemap]GitHub[/url]

Created using the [url=https://github.com/Whiskerwood-Modding/Whiskerwood-Project]Whiskerwood modkit[/url]."
	"changenote"		"1.1: The button now sits above the bottom toolbar and no longer shows over loading screens and menus. Removed the mod-menu setting."
